; Stripping lot details keeps a lot's "=" marker, part of the lot's identity.
;
; A fixated lot {=$5} and a floating lot {$5} bought on the same day are
; different lots (#1454), and --lots lists them apart.  --lot-prices
; (price only) and --lots-actual (only details written in the journal)
; show each lot as the lot that has only those details.  Ledger used to
; leave the marker out of them, so both lots became one lot, which was
; marked fixated: both reports showed a single 20 AAPL {=$5} lot, and the
; register showed the floating purchase as {=$5}.  Ledger now keeps the
; marker and leaves the floating lot unfixated, so the two lots stay apart
; in these reports, as they do under --lots.

2020/01/01 Fixated lot
    Assets:Broker               10 AAPL {=$5} [2020/01/01]
    Equity:Opening Balances

2020/01/01 Floating lot
    Assets:Broker               10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01]
    Equity:Opening Balances

test bal --lots Broker
 10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01]
10 AAPL {=$5} [2020/01/01]  Assets:Broker
end test

test bal --lot-prices Broker
        10 AAPL {$5}
       10 AAPL {=$5}  Assets:Broker
end test

test bal --lots-actual Broker
 10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01]
10 AAPL {=$5} [2020/01/01]  Assets:Broker
end test

test reg --lot-prices Broker
20-Jan-01 Fixated lot           Assets:Broker          10 AAPL {=$5} 10 AAPL {=$5}
20-Jan-01 Floating lot          Assets:Broker          10 AAPL {$5} 10 AAPL {$5}
                                                                   10 AAPL {=$5}
end test
